Consumer<T>
Takes one input (type T)
Does not return anything (void)
It’s used to perform an action (like printing, logging, saving, etc.)
accept() is the abstract method that performs the action.

import java.util.List;

public class ConsumerExample {

	public static void main(String[] args) {
		List<String> names = List.of("Murali", "Saravanan", "Selva");

		names.stream()
		     .map(s->s.toLowerCase())
		     .filter(s->s.length()<=5)
		     .forEach(System.out::println);  

	}

}
